                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Tanki Online is not just a game to me. It is a part of my childhood, a place where countless memories were made, and an experience that will always have a special place in my heart. There is something genuinely heartbreaking about realizing that a game you once played for hours without a care in the world has become a memory of a simpler time.\n\nI remember the excitement of joining a battle, the satisfaction of getting a new upgrade, and the happiness of finally unlocking something I had been working towards for weeks. Every match felt special, every victory felt earned, and even the defeats became memories worth keeping. It was never just about tanks, weapons, or ranks. It was about the feeling of being there.\n\nWhat makes Tanki Online so special is that it reminds me of a time when happiness was so simple. I didn't need impressive graphics, complicated stories, or massive open worlds. I just needed a tank, a battlefield, and a few hours of my life that I could spend enjoying something I genuinely loved.\n\nAnd perhaps that is the saddest part. You can return to the game, play the same maps, use the same weapons, and hear the same sounds, but you can never truly return to the person you were when you first discovered it. The game might still exist, but those moments, those afternoons, and that version of childhood are gone.\n\nTanki Online will always be more than a game to me. It is a time capsule of memories, a reminder of who I used to be, and a small piece of my childhood that I wish I could experience one more time.\n\nSome games entertain you. Others become a part of your life. Tanki Online was the latter.",
